==Strategy==
The restriction here shouldn't be too problematic as spamming units is generally not a viable option anyways thanks to the presence of Okame. Most strategies and units used for [[The Pure Land (Merciless)|The Pure Land]] will work just fine here, so long as one is very mindful of their unit presence on the field. As with the aforementioned stage, this stage is laser-focused on preserving ground, and thus the usage of [[Battle Items#Sniper the Cat|Sniper the Cat]] and Breakerblast are key to a successful run.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*Talented [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T.]]: C.A.T. is a menace on this stage. They're able to clear 2/3 peons with ease, are serviceable against the other (being [[Ginger Snache]]), and can score great amounts of damage against Okame. In addition, their ability to weaken prolongs their own lifeline, especially against Okame's attacks. At level 30 with full health talents, they're able to survive a hit from the boss, allowing them to land at least one near guaranteed hit. Do not use C.A.T if you don't have their talents, however; they'll be far too weak to do anything meaningful.
*[[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]]: Roe is a fantastic tanker for this stage. Their huge bulk paired with fast speed makes stalling Okame trivially easy, assuming no peons get in the way. Their weaken also provides great opportunity for other attackers to score more hits, so long as you get lucky with the procs.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]: Bullet Train works great on this stage. They can easily score big damage for quite cheap, in addition to getting double money on any peon it manages to kill. At level 37, they'll also have just enough health to survive a hit from Okame, allowing them to rebound for extra damage. This unit also benefits heavily from any unit that can weaken Okame, as with a weaken Bullet Train survives enough damage to usually land 3 hits.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]]: Boulder is a great staller for this stage. They're able to plug any gaps in the player's defenses rapidly, all whilst having a cheap cost and rapid cooldown. As always, Rock works best on this stage with various [[Cat Combo|research combos]], so long as the player is careful to not trigger Okame's attacks on accident.

